Revision history for Pipe-Declare

0.02    2026-06-20
        - Fix load failure on perl < 5.21.x (undefined symbols) for the
          MIN_PERL_VERSION 5.014 the dist already advertises. Three core API
          functions used by the XS are post-5.14 and not emulated by ppport.h:
          op_convert_list (5.21.6, -> Perl_convert), pad_findmy_pvn (5.15.1
          rename of pad_findmy), and op_sibling_splice (5.21.2), which is now
          backported on top of ppport.h's OpSIBLING/Op*SIB_set accessors.

0.01    2026-06-19
        First release.

        - `pipe { HEAD |> step |> step ... }` block keyword as a true
          lexical pragma (gated on $^H{'Pipe::Declare'}), works on
          perl 5.14+.
        - Global infix `|>` operator via PL_infix_plugin on perl 5.38+,
          registered at INFIX_PREC_LOGICAL_OR (same as `||` - tighter
          than `=`, looser than `+`). Left-associative; chains
          naturally. Lexically scoped on the same pragma.
        - Head forms: $var, literal, [LIST] arrayref, bareword call
          (qualified or not), (EXPR).
        - Step forms (block): bareword nullary, bareword with arglist
          (with `_` placeholder substitution), qualified bareword,
          \&name, sub { ... }, $cv, ->method, ->method(args), ->{KEY},
          ->[IDX], map / grep / tap blocks.
        - Step forms (infix): bareword call, method call, coderef
          expression. Block-only steps (map/grep/tap, _ placeholder,
          standalone ->method / ->{key} / ->[idx]) are block-form only.
        - Head evaluated exactly once.
        - Intermediate steps run in scalar context; final step inherits
          the surrounding context (scalar / list / void).
        - Specific croak messages for every parser-detected error.
        - Zero CPAN dependencies; core perl C API only, MIN_PERL 5.014.
        - 131 tests across t/00..t/10.

        Performance (perl 5.42, Apple Silicon; see xt/bench.pl):
        - Nest-when-safe lowering: when every step uses the topic
          exactly once (the common case), the pipe lowers to a fully
          nested call expression with no pad temp and no SASSIGN ops.
          Bench-measured within 1-2% of hand-written nested calls for
          bareword chains, call-with-args, and method chains.
        - SASSIGN-chain fallback: used only when a step references the
          topic 2+ times (e.g. `f(_, _, _)`); preserves intermediate-
          scalar-context semantics.
        - map / grep block steps build direct OP_MAPSTART / OP_GREPSTART
          optrees via op_convert_list; ~24% overhead remaining is the
          cost of wrapping each map/grep result in [ ... ] to keep the
          topic as an arrayref across steps.

